Flags
--n         N number
--k-start   first K to start sieve or single number test
--k-end     last K to stop sievie
--pstart    min 50000000000
--pmax      default min.50000000000
--workers   numbers of threads
--report    in %, default 25%, 0=only result, e.g [STEP] k=843 -> 25% | Max Err: 2.93e-03
--out-primes  out primes to file autosave is to primes.txt, put your file name
--out-sieve   out candidates after presieve, put your file name
--in-file     loading candidates to continue presiesieve, or test from file
--sieve-only  abord before FFT proth test

this algorithm test one number = one thread

Single number test, no needed sieve but default setings are always set:

